---
import { Aside, Code } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';
---

<div class="property-section">
  <Code code={`"channels": [{ "id": "myChannel", "type": "string" }]`} lang="json" />
  <p>
    Each entry in a widget's <code>channels</code> array accepts a <code>type</code> key specifying the channel's data
    type. Can be <code>"number"</code> (the default) for numeric values or <code>"string"</code> for text values.
  </p>
  <p>String channels are first-class state in the backend:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Values sent from the UI with <code>sendControlData()</code> are stored on the channel (and into the matching
      Csound string channel, readable with the string variant of <code>cabbageGetValue</code>).
    </li>
    <li>
      String values are included in session and preset saves, and re-pushed to the UI in the launch widget dumps, which
      makes string channels the mechanism for persisting custom interface state across UI reloads. See
      <a href="/docs/custom-ui/persisting-ui-state/">Persisting Custom UI State</a>.
    </li>
    <li>String channels are excluded from DAW automation (automation requires numeric channels).</li>
  </ul>
  <Aside>
    <p>
      The operative key is the per-channel <code>type</code> inside <code>channels[]</code>, not a widget-level
      property.
    </p>
  </Aside>
</div>
